WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 31 - The One-Woman Show

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.580
A Passing Shower

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.680
So sleepy...

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.990
I'm getting up.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:53.380
No, don't pull the covers off me!

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.690
Thanks for coming!

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.940
Dad, can you please stop reading the paper in the bathroom?

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.460
Sheesh...

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:14.760
What's she doing?

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.610
Brushing her teeth.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.060
Morning, Mom!

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.470
That smells delicious!

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:36.210
You can practically see her family around her!

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.860
I'm soaked through.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.450
Man...

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.040
I hope it stops soon.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.520
It's been so rainy this year.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.510
Oh look, it's Dad!

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:59.930
But who's that with him?

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.100
What's going on?

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:02.950
I don't know that woman...

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.760
Stop talking!

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.770
Oh Dad, don't look at her like that.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:09.310
She's giving him an ultimatum!

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.540
Stop it! Stop crying!

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.970
You're going to convince him if you keep crying like that!

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.660
Dad, what's wrong? Why aren't you saying anything?

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.750
Shake your head already!

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:32.310
Why's she dragging her feet like that?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:40.630
I can't believe he ended up saying yes.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.140
He nodded!

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.220
The rain's so cold!

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.210
I can feel its chill when I look at her expression.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:57.860
I'm going to get my father and my family back.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.810
That woman...

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:06.440
She said she wanted him to meet her parents in Kanazawa...

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:09.920
on his next day off and my Dad... he actually agreed to do so!

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.060
Liar!

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.650
He promised he'd take us for a day out on his next day off!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.340
What have we ever done to deserve this?

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.640
Mom's always cooking his favorite dishes for him.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:34.670
She irons his shirts and everything - so why's he trying to throw us away?

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:40.640
Hi Dad! I'm sorry to bother you at work.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.240
No, everything's fine, I just...

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.250
I got the urge to come see you.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:56.670
Hey, why don't I make you some sushi for your birthday?

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.980
That'd be great, wouldn't it, Dad?

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.200
Dad?

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.740
What's wrong, Dad?

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.730
Why aren't you laughing?

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:11.000
Hey Dad...

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:15.100
you <i>are</i> taking us all out on a road trip on your next day off, aren't you?

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.300
You're taking us out somewhere, aren't you?

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.020
Dad?

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.930
Really? That's great!

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.110
Then, I'll pack us all a picnic!

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.580
I'll make your favorite: fried chicken.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.810
See you later, Dad!

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:55.230
But it's not like Dad said he'd leave that woman...

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.220
What am I going to do?

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:58.720
What should I do?

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:06.090
I didn't come here to drink tea with you.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.960
I want you to stop seeing my father.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.300
Right now.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.350
You say you're sorry?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.870
Well, if you're really sorry, then you can just leave him alone, can't you?

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:20.530
You say you love him?! Please, this isn't a joke!

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:25.450
You know, my Dad reads the paper on the toilet every morning!

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.910
Did you know <i>that</i> about him? Bet you didn't!

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.160
He wears long johns and does that exercise routine on the radio...

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.430
He's such a dork!

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:37.110
He's really uncool...

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.140
An arranged marriage?

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:57.410
You say you're going to leave him anyway?

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.270
You're going to find someone else to marry...

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.560
and everything will return to normal?

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:09.240
I'm off now.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.510
Thank you very much.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.480
Everything's back the way it's always been.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:24.110
I didn't even notice that it stopped raining.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:28.110
The roads are really wet right now, but tomorrow, the sun will come out...

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:31.300
and everything will dry up again.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:37.910
A passing shower... that's what this was today - a small cloudburst passing overhead.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:42.480
I bet that's how Dad felt, too.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.060
I'm starving.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.870
Oh, it's really late!

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:48.970
Mom's going to be really ticked off!

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:51.810
I'm home!

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:03.540
Just for a moment, I was able to live the life of a girl with a happy family.

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:08.410
I still have Hiromi Satou's memories inside me.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:11.580
They're happy and warm.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.220
What?

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.590
You want me to perform in a play for the Theater Club?!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.300
That's fantastic! But what about the rules...

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:23.740
Well, I can't let you in as a full member because you used to be a pro,

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:26.770
but there's nothing in the rules to stop you from performing as a guest.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.060
Great!

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:33.370
Mr. Masumi just wanted you to know that Ms. Tsukikage is getting...

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:36.550
the very best care she can at the hospital, so you don't have to worry about her.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.470
Here's her medical report.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.370
What's wrong?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:45.350
Mr. Masumi promised he'd keep you updated about her condition, didn't he?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.850
Well, I didn't think he'd keep it.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:54.680
Once he makes a promise, he never breaks it.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:04.580
Why did I phone Masumi Hayami when Ms. Tsukikage collapsed?

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:07.630
I should hate him more than anyone else in the world.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.260
It's right over there.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.510
Mr. Hayami!

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:17.330
My car's in the garage.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:18.940
I don't have a long way to go.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.390
Sir, I must apologize - I forgot your umbrella.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:26.200
You can share mine. It's my thanks...

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:28.980
for all the help you've given to Ms. Tsukikage.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:32.890
Thank you.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.180
But this is a man's job.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.730
It's nice to walk in the snow.

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:45.440
I wouldn't have expected you to enjoy such a simple pleasure.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.920
I like the snow.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.940
It's weird. He looks like a completely different person.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.190
Sometimes, I just don't understand him.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:57.020
Are you lovebirds on a date?!

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:59.230
All kissy-kissy, smoochy-smoochy, yeah?

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.870
Excuse me!

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.880
Wait up, little one!

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:06.810
You idiot.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:08.110
You have to watch the lights!

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:09.530
It's on red!

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:25.730
Thanks for taking care of her, but don't think that means I think you're a good person now!

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:36.590
There's always a red light between me and her.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:39.090
No matter how much time passes, I can't seem to cross over to her side.{bleh at red light metaphor}

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.850
Tonight is Ayumi's opening night for her one-woman show.

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.410
Miss!

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.560
Sakurakouji!

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.480
What's wrong, Sakurakouji?

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:00.770
The show's about to start!

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:01.690
Yeah...

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:10.100
Ayumi's show's starting.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:13.040
Ayumi Himekawa's
<i>Juliet</i>

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:18.040
Ayumi Himekawa's One-Woman Performance of <i>Juliet</i> is a Runaway Success!

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:23.040
We would like to congratulate you on the success of your show, Juliet.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.620
Thank you very much.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.710
I'm relieved that the opening night went so well.

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:30.830
Some say that you are challenging Shakespeare himself with this interpretation.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:34.410
The only thing I've challenged with this piece is myself.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.150
It's made me very happy that I was able to succeed.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:40.320
She's so far ahead of me again.

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:43.170
How can I possibly even come close to that?

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:47.910
Please walk towards me as Lulu the Robot.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:48.520
Affirmative.

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:00.350
Stop.

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:10.600
Please pick up that handkerchief.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.640
I never expected such a turnout!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:33.830
Did you call for me, Master?

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.730
Please relax.

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.890
I apologize for having kept you waiting.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.730
That went really well!

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:57.090
You made this happen, Kitajima.

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.830
I've never seen an audience enjoying themselves as much as they did tonight.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:03.970
You've taught us a lot with your acting.

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:10.060
I'm glad I got into acting.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.880
This is the only thing I'm good at.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.890
I really love acting.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.140
Miss Kitajima!

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:18.910
Someone has sent you flowers!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.410
Purple roses?!

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.710
Please still be here!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.530
It's the man who left those roses!

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:36.600
Please wait!

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:40.590
I'm finally meeting him!

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:44.290
You're Mr. Purple Roses, aren't you? The man who keeps sending me purple roses?

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:48.080
You don't know how grateful I am for all you've done for me.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:52.050
Whenever I've felt down, you've helped me out so much and...

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.640
I'm not the man you're looking for.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:59.020
Someone asked me to drop off these flowers.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.030
That's all.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:01.320
But, that can't be!

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.220
I was so happy that we finally met.

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:07.500
You said someone asked you to drop them off, right?

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:11.020
Can you please tell me about that man?

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:13.730
He's a wonderful person.

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:17.260
I'm sorry, but I'm not at liberty to divulge any further information about him.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:23.780
If I ever get another chance to get up on stage, I want to talk to him directly.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:28.180
If I'm ever in another big production, I want to invite him personally!

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:31.570
What should I do?

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.130
It's my dream to meet him...

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:37.780
If you promise not to make any inquiries into his identity,

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:40.770
then I will act as a messenger for you.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:44.760
But you mustn't tell anyone else about me.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:47.610
Even if you see me in town, you mustn't speak to me.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:51.610
If we randomly meet, then you must pretend that you don't even know me.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:56.120
Karato Hijiri

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:54.200
Can you promise me that?

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.120
I promise!

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:58.840
Karato Hijiri...

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:02.220
Okay. I promise I won't try to find out who he is.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:06.850
After all, there's now a bridge that connects me and Mr. Purple Roses.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:12.350
I gave my name to Maya Kitajima, but your identity remains secret.

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:18.900
It's her dream to invite "Mr. Purple Roses" to her next big production if she's ever in another one.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:21.290
What an honor.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:28.380
Hijiri, my father, the CEO, and I are the only two people who know you.

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:33.730
You and your father have agreed to live in the shadow of Daito Entertainment.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:37.180
You've dedicated your life to it, and for that, I am very grateful.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:41.620
My father would have killed himself and his whole family twenty years ago...

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:45.560
if it wasn't for your father, the President of Daito Entertainment.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.540
I was sure at that point that I was a dead man walking,

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:50.930
so now, I am ready to serve and repay my debt.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:53.980
With my life, if necessary.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:56.310
Juliet?! No, I won't!

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:58.250
I wanted to thank you for giving me your umbrella.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:02.090
If you don't want to come and see it with me, I can just drop you off at the theater.

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:05.800
Are you scared to see Ayumi's play, little one?

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:09.280
Or maybe you believe that you're much too talented to bother with a meager threat...

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.010
like Ayumi Himekawa?

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:14.300
Fine, I'll go!

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:16.270
Why's he always so sarcastic?

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:23.900
He's cast himself in the role of the villain for Maya's sake.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.370
You really think so?

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:34.140
Mr. Masumi, I regret to inform you that we have no more seats available!

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:35.980
It doesn't matter. We'll stand.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:48.590
She's a bird.

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:51.210
She flew!

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:57.270
She's different from all the other times I've seen her before.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:17:00.750
What an elegant and dazzling Juliet!

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:04.730
Come hither, sweet lark! Come hither, sweet friend!

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.730
She sat down on a chair!

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:18.160
When I conceived that mine fingers had grasped joy...

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:21.680
it slipp'd betwixt them once more.

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:25.750
Such is how happiness evades capture.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:30.260
O dear larks. Thou art undeniably free.

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:40.880
O Romeo, swear not by the moon!

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:46.340
Th'inconstant moon that monthly changes in her circle orb!

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:50.810
Ayumi is constantly honing her talent.

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:55.230
She's so far ahead of me. I can't even compete with her.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:58.230
I'm not even close to being on her level.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.660
What are you doing here, Maya?

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:08.630
Please tutor me.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:12.340
Even if only for a little while!

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.640
I want to improve!

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:16.630
To become better than Ayumi?

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.060
Yes.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:24.880
You saw her show, <i>Juliet</i>, didn't you?

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.850
I want you to try and act out a scene. Right now.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.130
Do it! This is a rehearsal!

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:48.490
That felt like a passel of heavy bags getting dropped off!

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:54.580
Come hither, sweet lark! Come hither, sweet friend!

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:03.580
An actor isn't worth a dime if they can't control their own body.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:06.190
Ayumi was amazing.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:11.030
Her Juliet saw herself soaring through the clouds with the lark that flew away.

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:13.190
It was exquisite.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.390
The lark that flew away...

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:28.900
"When I conceived that mine fingers had grasped joy... it slipp'd betwixt them once more."

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:33.900
"Such is how happiness evades capture."

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:39.340
"O dear larks."

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:42.980
"Thou art undeniably free."

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:45.600
Why did you put your hands behind your back just then?

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:52.860
Because Juliet has no wings nor freedom, so she became envious...

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:59.600
of the larks. That's why she just put her hands behind her back.

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:02.820
You think she's envious of the larks?

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:06.280
Sorry... Is that an odd interpretation of the scene?

00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:12.860
Well, compared to Ayumi's polished performance, it was pretty amateur.

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:19.810
Ayumi!

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:22.880
Ms. Tsukikage, I'm sorry I interrupted.

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.870
It's not a problem.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:27.940
After all, we set up a meeting for this time.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:33.010
She knew Ayumi was going to show up here. That's why she made Maya rehearse Juliet's lines.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:38.970
I can't believe Ayumi just witnessed my pathetic performance!

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:42.400
You think she's envious of the larks?

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:44.530
What a frightening girl.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:47.480
Your instincts frighten me.

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:50.470
Why did you do that?

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:55.490
I wanted Maya to realize her current level of skill.

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:57.670
What do you think is the main differences between those two?

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.040
I couldn't tell you.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.180
Confidence and fighting spirit.

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:04.810
Something Ayumi has and Maya doesn't.

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:07.770
Ayumi Himekawa is truly spectacular...

00:21:07.770 --> 00:21:10.700
and there's nothing holding her back from performing in <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.000
Ms. Tsukikage...

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:15.370
Maya needs to improve drastically.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:18.880
Can I just ask you one question?

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:24.440
What do you think about Maya's talent as an actress?

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:27.880
Talent? You're asking me about her talent for acting?

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.940
Maya Kitajima...

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:33.880
is nothing short of a genius.

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:44.600
Now that she has been shown the gulf in talent between herself and Ayumi,

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:47.260
will Maya be able to overcome her own disappointment and head towards...

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:49.790
the Scarlet Angel once more?

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
Chikazukitai noni toozaketeshimau

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
I want to be close to you, but you're distancing yourself.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
Dakishimetai toki wazato hanareteshimau

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
When I want to hold you, you deliberately run away.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
Marude jishaku no N to N no you da ne

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
We're like two poles on a magnet...

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Otagai amari nimo nisugita seikana?

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Maybe we're too alike?

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
Motto motto sunao na hitomi de mitsureba

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
If you allow your eyes to see the truth,

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
Yodonderu izumi mo suki tooru hazusa

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
even quagmires will become crystal clear.

00:23:22.900 --> 00:23:26.820
Ms. Tsukikage, are you serious?

00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:31.930
You're saying that if Maya doesn't get the same award within the next two years,

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:34.570
I'll be the one chosen to play the lead in <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>?

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:38.530
No, I'm sure she'll do it.

00:23:39.140 --> 00:23:43.100
I won't let my guard down. I'll maintain my work rate.

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:48.260
I'll fulfill my childhood dream under my own steam!

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 32 - A Midsummer Night's Dream
